WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.413
Next, which cloud.

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:05.725
Every command reads the cloud from the
settings file, one name per provider.

3
00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:11.089
The estate this runbook writes for is
Microsoft 365 G C C with commercial Azure,

4
00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:14.802
so Graph and Resource Manager
are the worldwide hosts,

5
00:00:14.802 --> 00:00:18.350
as Microsoft Learn's national
cloud page lists them.

6
00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.960
Oracle Cloud takes its
commercial or government realm,

7
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.825
AWS its commercial or GovCloud partition,
and Google Cloud its global name.

8
00:00:26.825 --> 00:00:30.041
As a side note, G C C High
and the Defense Department

9
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:33.650
cloud sign in to Graph with
their own environment names.

10
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.940
Any other name throws, and a session
signed in elsewhere is refused.
